{
  "version": 1,
  "about": [
    "The Genesis Brands look-and-feel asset kit. Three catalogues — eight forced-choice pairs,",
    "nine palettes and four type specimens — behind the taste questions of the Purpose Playbook",
    "discovery questionnaire (knowledge/layer1/modules/intake/purpose-playbook-signals.yaml,",
    "Act 5).",
    "",
    "Everything here is presentation and fact: what the client sees, and the hexes and faces an",
    "agent needs to actually produce a palette or set a word. What a choice MEANS is reasoning",
    "and lives in knowledge/layer1/modules/directions/look-and-feel-kit.yaml, keyed by the same",
    "values. Nothing here is a screenshot or a real brand: every specimen is originated.",
    "",
    "Tile labels never name a design attribute ('serif', 'asymmetric'). A client who is told",
    "what they are looking at answers with the word, not the taste. The design term is carried",
    "separately in each option's `form`, for the agents and the designer."
  ],

